  "remove_from_shared_pages": [
    "field-catalog.md sections benchmark-payload and evaluation-verdict (replace with links)",
    "field-contracts.json: types MetricObservation, MissingEvidence, MetricFinding are no longer used by these contracts. Remove them if no other contract uses them.",
    "other-contracts.md rows benchmark_payload.json and evaluation_verdict.json",
    "examples/baseline_execution.txt, treatment_execution.txt, provisioning_example.txt are kept only as synthetic stdout and provisioning files referenced by the new receipts. They are no longer contracts.",
    "examples/science_guard_profile.json: criterion registered_rule_applied is replaced by the host check rule_recomputation. Update or retire the file and the science_* review examples.",
    "examples/evaluation_capsule.json: old declaration left unchanged. scientific_evaluation_capsule.json replaces it. Other science_* files still reference the old name."
  ],
  "prd_conflicts": [
    "PRD 3.7.2 says run the baseline first, followed immediately by the treatment. M1 runs all baseline repeats, then all treatment repeats, one block each. This is a reading, not a conflict.",
    "PRD 3.8.2 asks Evaluation to audit metric values against raw stdout and stderr. M1 does this as the deterministic Benchmark check values_match_empirical_results, and Evaluation reads only the admitted payload."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Changed shared field contracts: benchmark-payload 1 to 2 and evaluation-verdict 1 to 2. Delivery examples (delivery_manifest*.json, delivery_capsule.json) reference the old sha256 values and the old field limitations. Delivery owner must refresh both. The bytes of evaluation_verdict.json and benchmark_payload.json changed.",
    "Hypothesis blueprint sha256 in my examples is the current blueprint v2 file. Re-run the hash refresh if the blueprint changes again.",
    "poc_artifact_bundle has no field contract of its own. The declaration port uses poc-manifest:field-contract:1 with the bundle named by archive_ref. Builder owner may define a separate ID.",
    "The Benchmark CC reads no outcome_rules. Confirm Hypothesis owner keeps seed_policy fixed_same_for_all_runs in M1, since per-run seeds depend on it.",
    "Baseline failure halts the run for human triage. A treatment failure is recorded as an unmeasured metric. Confirm with the PRD owner.",
    "aggregation_rule m1_conjunctive_v1 treats all registered metrics as one conjunctive claim and makes every metric required. Confirm the PRD owner accepts that FAIL outranks INCONCLUSIVE.",
    "plausibility implausible forces INCONCLUSIVE. This model judgement overrides rule results. Confirm the PRD owner wants it to block, since PRD 3.8.3 only says to flag anomalies."
  ]
}